This pipeline bundles unmodified source code from the nf-core/modules repository
(https://github.com/nf-core/modules), which is distributed under the MIT License.
The vendored files are located under modules/nf-core/ and are pinned to the
revision below. Per-module authors and maintainers are recorded in each module's
meta.yml; tool licences are recorded there as well under tools.<tool>.licence.

Vendored revision:

    https://github.com/nf-core/modules.git
    commit efec54255f9baad3ea032173d75031929883bed8

Vendored modules:

    modules/nf-core/bwa/index
    modules/nf-core/bwa/mem
    modules/nf-core/samtools/faidx
    modules/nf-core/pairtools/parse
    modules/nf-core/pairtools/sort
    modules/nf-core/pairtools/merge
    modules/nf-core/pairtools/dedup
    modules/nf-core/pairtools/split
    modules/nf-core/pairtools/select
    modules/nf-core/cooler/cload
    modules/nf-core/cooler/zoomify
    modules/nf-core/cooler/merge

The local module modules/local/calder2/ is derived from the nf-core/modules calder2
module (MIT) at the revision above. It adds an optional feature_track input so a
Nextflow-staged A/B phasing BED can be passed to CALDER.

The local module modules/local/cooler_balance/ is derived from the nf-core/modules
cooler/balance module (MIT) at the revision above. It copies the input cooler to the
output path instead of symlinking it, so balancing never modifies its declared input
and the task is idempotent on -resume.

The local modules modules/local/bwamem2_index/ and modules/local/bwamem3_index/ are
derived from the nf-core/modules bwamem2/index and bwamem3/index modules (MIT) at the
revision above. They replace the memory directive with a reference-size model plus
headroom (bwa-mem3 uses its documented 16/24 bytes per genome base).

The local modules modules/local/bwamem2_mem/ and modules/local/bwamem3_mem/ are
derived from the nf-core/modules bwamem2/mem and bwamem3/mem modules (MIT) at the
revision above. They replace the process_high label with an inline memory directive
that scales with the staged index size, because mem holds the index resident.

The subworkflow subworkflows/local/ontad/ and the local modules
modules/local/ontad_dump_matrix/, modules/local/ontad/ and
modules/local/ontad_assemble/, together with the helper scripts bin/ontad_*.py, are
original nf-hic code. They call OnTAD (https://github.com/anlin00007/OnTAD), which is
distributed under the MIT License. OnTAD is not packaged in bioconda, so
modules/local/ontad/ runs from the patched v1.4 container image
ghcr.io/snsinfu/anlin00007-ontad:v1.4-p3.

